# --- ROMs and saves --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# First, because it is the only rule here that cannot be fixed later. A ROM committed once stays
# in the history after it is deleted, and only rewriting history removes it.
#
# BanjoCoop never ships, downloads or contains a ROM. Players supply their own to BanjoRecompiled,
# which copies it into its own config folder — and on this machine that copy lives under run/,
# which is ignored below. These patterns are the second line of defence for one dropped anywhere
# else in the tree.
*.z64
*.n64
*.v64
*.rom
*.sra
*.eep
*.mpk
*.bin

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
build-native/
dist/

# --- fetched or built by scripts/bootstrap.sh --------------------------------------------------
#
# The BanjoRecompiled release (21 MB, GPL-3, not ours to keep in this history) and RecompModTool,
# which is built from the vendor/N64Recomp submodule. Both are reproducible, so neither belongs
# in the repo.
runtime/
tools/RecompModTool

# --- play-test state ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Logs, save snapshots, and the whole second game instance — which contains an imported ROM and
# save files. Everything here is the product of playing the game, not of building it.
run/

# --- editor / OS -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
